    "yearsExperience": "2+",
    "bio": "DVM graduate and MS researcher in Microbiology and Hygiene, with research experience in molecular biology, virology, and viral genomics. My research combines experimental and computational approaches to study pathogen biology, host–pathogen interactions, and molecular mechanisms of disease. Seeking for PhD in molecular biology and related fields.\n",
    "researchInterests": "My PhD research interests center on the molecular evolution and phylodynamics of avian and zoonotic RNA/DNA viruses — particularly reassortment, recombination, and selection pressure driving emergence in poultry-dense, high-spillover-risk regions like South Asia. I am seeking a PhD lab with strengths in viral genomics, computational evolutionary biology, and One Health surveillance, where field-derived data can be paired with rigorous bioinformatic modeling.",
    "researchPhilosophy": "I approach a problem by first going to the source — the outbreak, the sample, the raw sequencing read — before trusting any downstream model. Field diagnostics taught me that clean data beats clever statistics, and computational virology taught me that a phylogeny is only as honest as the quality control behind it. I try to hold both instincts at once: hands willing to do the bench work, and a mind that stays skeptical of its own pipeline.",
    "currentResearch": "Fowl adenovirus",
